concerns.note:
The plan has no risks_and_assumptions content, and the standard_v1 shape and risk-coverage criterion expect one. It leaves several assumptions unstated:
- the accepted `idle_since` format: the plan only shows `24h`, and Go's time.ParseDuration has no day unit;
- the response to a malformed or negative value: this should be a 400, not a silent no-filter result;
- how the filter combines with existing GET /v0/runs filters and pagination;
- whether the query is indexed on stage updated_at, since it aggregates the latest stage update per run, which may be a full scan on large tables;
- workspace or tenant scoping of the new query.
No acceptance criterion covers invalid input.
